==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Miss Moneko''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Superstar Moneko''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
As Moneko is very slow and has short-ranged attacks, she'll be inefficient in most stages as her 15% chance of Critical will rarely be enough, but she can at least kill the [[CyberFace]] in [[Steel Visage (Deadly)|Steel Visage]] if nothing better is available. Her main use comes from her Combos, as [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]] offers a good damage improvement for just 2 units. It can also be combined with [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]], who might easily be in the army regardless for an extra [[Worker Cat]] level which never hurts. If Sister Act is combined with another 2-slot attack Combo like [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]], the resulting damage boost (+20%) will be higher than using 4 slots for an Attack Up (M) instead (+15%).

With appropriate timing and planning, Moneko can be useful in early stages that feature 1-2 [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies and can even be used against [[Super Metal Hippoe]]. However, she is easily outclassed by any [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] obtained through the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]], as well as [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] drops such as [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]], [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]] and even [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
What this True Form offers is too little too late, especially for its price. It gives her a mini-wave, reduces her recharge time, and improves her Critical Hit chance a little. Superstar Moneko still loses out against competing alternatives by the time it is obtainable and mostly acts as a trophy of game progression. She can still help against [[Metal Doge]]s, [[Croconator]]s, [[Koronium]]s and, to a degree, [[Metal One Horn]]s, if necessary. Her Critical mini-waves do have a niche in mixed stages, as she doesn't need to specifically target a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy for her mini-wave to take them out. She is also somewhat viable at clearing Metal peons on {{4c}} stages in place of [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]]. Granted, with her low attack stat and horrible range, this niche is unreliable and only useful in a few stages.

Regarding the materials needed to evolve Moneko, the earliest you can obtain a Gold Catfruit Seed is directly after beating [[Infernal Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] of the [[Infernal Tower]], which is the only place to drop it. By this point in the game, you are are likely to have much better units that can deliver Critical Hits, and there are much better uses for the seeds you obtain from the stage.

