==Trivia==
*Moneko had several improvements before the game had the current English Version:
**[[Version 2.3 Update|Version 2.3]] reduced her base recharge time from 3,600f<sup>120s</sup> to 1,998f<sup>66.6s</sup>, granted her a 10% chance to do Critical Hits, and increased her Evolved Form's base health from 600 to 1,000.
**[[Version 2.4 Update|Version 2.4]] buffed her Critical Hit chance to 15%.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Moneko was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[The Divas (Removed Combo)|The Divas]].
*Moneko and [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Bean Cats]] were the only two Cat Units needing [[Invite Friends to get Moneko|Invitation Codes]] to unlock until [[Version 4.3 Update|Version 4.3]] removed the feature.
*She is the first unit to have her own unique death animation.
*The ''neko'' in Moneko's, [[Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Neneko]]'s and [[Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Koneko]]'s names means ''cat'', likely meant to represent the fact that they are ''[[wikipedia:Catgirl|Nekomimi]]'', or people with the ears and tail of a cat.
*Unlike [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], she isn't considered a [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] as she can be upgraded to level 40 even before clearing [[An Ancient Curse]].
*In the Japanese Version, Superstar Moneko's stage says her name on it, but in all other versions, it's replaced with stars. The change was likely made to avoid having to change the text between different languages.
*Moneko's color scheme is consistent across games. Her yellow blouse in [[Monster Hunter Collaboration Event|Monster Hunter]] was carried over to [[Nyanko Defence Force]] and [[Go! Go! Pogo Cat]], and Miss Moneko's pink dress and blue-and-green accessories in [[Merc Storia Collaboration Event|Merc Storia]] were kept for Nyanko Defence Force and partly included in Superstar Moneko's design.
*Moneko had a third form in Nyanko Defence Force three years prior to the introduction of Superstar Moneko, although it was just a simple palette-swap with two more lights added to her stage.
*One of the possible endings for [[Gamatoto Expedition]] log messages is "after meeting Moneko."
*In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], there is an error in her preview screen stating she can be unlocked when clearing all "Into the Future" stages rather than all "Empire of Cats" stages.
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Moneko's name in her Evolved and True Form was capitalized. Additionally, her Normal Form and Evolved Form descriptions were altered, originally reading:
<pre>Moneko
Hoping to become an idol.
She sings on the streets everyday.
You might see her around, please say hi.</pre>
<pre>Miss MONEKO
Thanks to everyone, she made it to stardom!
Now she's everyone's favorite star!
Please support her! The future is still bright!</pre>

